course: dictionary
lesson: 12653
title: Disregarded: paying no attention
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Disregarded means ignored, or not paid attention to. When you disregard something, you push it aside as if it does not matter. Disregard is a verb, so its forms are disregard, disregards, disregarded and disregarding.
explain: «She disregarded the warning and walked onto the thin ice.» She saw the warning, but she chose not to pay attention to it. The sentence tells you she was in danger, because ignoring a warning is risky.
explain: In maths and science, «Air resistance may be disregarded» means you can leave it out of your working. The word is formal, so in everyday speech people usually say ignored.
fact: Disregarded means ignored or not paid attention to.
fact: With a formal meaning, disregarded can mean treated as not important, as in «The committee disregarded the old plan.»
fact: «He disregarded the warning sign» means he ignored it, which can be dangerous.
fact: Ignored is the everyday word for disregarded; overlooked and brushed aside are close in meaning.
fact: Disregard is a verb, so its past form is disregarded.
exercise: «He disregarded the warning sign and went onto the thin ice.» What does disregarded mean? | Lost it on the way home | Read it carefully and obeyed it | *Ignored, did not pay attention to it | Painted it bright red
exercise: «Air resistance may be disregarded in this calculation.» In maths, what does this tell you? | You must add it to every answer | You must measure it first | *You can leave it out of your working | It is the answer you must write
exercise: «The coach disregarded the rain and kept training.» Find and copy the word that means ignored. | coach | training | rain | *disregarded
test: «The judge disregarded the rumour because there was no proof.» What does disregarded mean here? | *Ignored, treated as not important | Believed every word of it | Repeated it to the crowd | Wrote it down in ink
test: Mum says, «Please don't disregard your homework.» What is she asking you to do? | *Pay attention to it and do it | Leave it for someone else | Put it in the bin | Copy the first word you see
exam: Which word best replaces disregarded in «He disregarded the sign»? | *Ignored | Obeyed | Copied | Read
